\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. O lord, how happy should we be
\par If we could cast our care on Thee,
\par If we from self could rest,
\par And feel at hand that One above,
\par In perfect wisdom, perfect love,
\par Is working for the best.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. How far from this our daily life,
\par Ever disturbed by anxious strife,
\par By sudden wild alarms.
\par O could we but relinquish all
\par Our earthly props, and simply fall
\par On Thine almighty arms.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Could we but kneel and cast our load,
\par E'en while we pray, upon our God'
\par Then rise with lightened cheer,
\par Sure that the Father, who is nigh
\par To still the famished raven's cry,
\par Will hear, in that we fear.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Lord, make these faithless hearts of ours
\par Thy lessons learn from birds and flowers:
\par Make them from self to cease,
\par Leave all things to a Father's will,
\par And taste, before Him lying still,
\par E'en in affliction, peace.
\par 
\par 
\par 
\par 
\par 
